[h1]Living Fellows[/h1]
[b]You won't die... alone.[/b]

[url=https://thorelvin.github.io/living-fellows/]Read the Field Guide[/url] | [url=https://thorelvin.github.io/living-fellows/quick-reference.html]Quick reference[/url] | [url=https://discord.gg/vPK7faQVt]Discord[/url] | [url=https://github.com/thorelvin/living-fellows/issues/new/choose]Report a bug[/url]

Living Fellows adds companions, survivor households and working bases to Project Zomboid. Find your people, give them somewhere to live and try to bring everyone home.

[h2]Send a squad on an expedition[/h2]
Scout a building, search for supplies, fish or collect wood while you get on with your own plans. Choose one to four companions, a leader, a walking or driving route and a return time. Watch their trip in a second view. They use real tools, collect real items and carry the haul into camp storage.

Wood crews find nearby woodland, borrow an axe and return logs to permitted Log Yard, Construction or General storage. Collected, carried and stored counts stay separate. A full store pauses delivery and retries automatically; manual Retry remains available.

[h2]Keep the camp working with Base Watch[/h2]
Leave an indoor resident on watch so the camp stays loaded while you travel. The others keep sorting, farming, cooking, repairing and guarding. Check in by radio while you're away. Base Watch and expeditions share one companion view, so run one at a time.

[h2]Call Markus's taxi[/h2]
Stranded on the road? Call for pickup from a working walkie-talkie, climb into Markus Sloane's cab and choose a road destination on the world map. Bring jewelry for the fare.

[h2]Build a crew worth knowing[/h2]
[list]
[*]Up to 16 persistent companions with professions, personalities, relationships, memories, needs, wounds and permanent death.
[*]Squad travel, combat rules, real equipment and medical care. Fellows fight together, treat injuries and retreat when they're outmatched.
[*]Private diaries written about things their owners actually experienced. The book stays behind when its author dies.
[*]Working bases with marked storage, jobs, construction, farming, cooking, logging and care for the dead. Blocked jobs pause and retry.
[*]Households that trade, offer work and remember how you treat them, plus 65 Strange Folk with their own stories. Random eligible encounters can begin on the second day.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Install [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3619862853]ZombieBuddy[/url] 2.3.3 or newer and complete its one-time loader setup. Subscribing alone is not enough.
[*]Subscribe to Living Fellows and enable both mods. For an existing save, use More... > Choose Mods too.
[*]Press Home to open the companion panel, or click LF. Meet a survivor and choose Recruit when offered.
[*]Use Orders, Squad, Expeditions and More > Base, or right-click the world for Living Fellows commands.
[/olist]

[b]Release 0.26.67. Project Zomboid Build 42.21.0, single-player.[/b] Multiplayer and additional human split-screen players are not supported.

The [url=https://github.com/thorelvin/living-fellows/releases/latest]Windows standalone edition[/url] includes its own bridge and needs no ZombieBuddy. Choose Workshop or standalone; use one copy at a time.

Need a hand? More > Support provides a diagnostic report. Include it, the game and mod versions, and what happened when reporting a problem.

